          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: പൂവ്",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "പൂവ് (pūvŭ) — \"a flower\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Proto-Dravidian pū, one of the shortest words the family has and one of the best kept: Tamil பூ, Telugu పువ్వు, Kannada ಹೂವು. Kannada's h is that opening shift again, met first at the fruit."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Kerala puts the word to work at the front of a compound: the flower-carpet laid out for the harvest festival is പൂക്കളം, the flower plus a word for a laid-out ground."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Malayalam's own form adds a v and the half-vowel, which is why it looks longer than Tamil's bare two letters while saying the same thing."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Four. A door, a chair, the pattern at the threshold, a flower."
            }
