          "title": "You'll want to know: മാല",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "മാല (māla) — \"a garland\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Sanskrit mālā, a garland or a string of things, borrowed all across the south. Kannada's ಹೂಮಾಲೆ (hūmāle) is this word with the flower-word stuck on the front of it, so the Kannada compound spells out what Malayalam leaves to context."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The word is also a string in the abstract — a series, a row — which is why a rosary and a necklace and a list can all be one."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "And that closes the door: the way in, the seat, the pattern on the ground, the flower and the garland. A guest arriving at a Kerala house in the old way would meet all five before a word was exchanged."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Five, and the run is closed: a door, a chair, the pattern at the threshold, a flower, a garland."
            }
          ]
        },
